  "text_pages": [
    "Welcome to Kyungsung University(**)\n스킵네비게이션\n본문바로가기\n주메뉴바로가기\n페이스북\n인스타\n유투브\n이전\n재생\n정지\n다음\nDon't be afraid of change. Prepare for the new era.\nA university specializing in Visual image & CT(Cultural Technology) and\noffering a practical education that will prepare you for life after graduation.\nKyungsung University is a university on the move.\nDon't be afraid of change. Prepare for the new era.\nA university specializing in Visual image & CT(Cultural Technology) and\noffering a practical education that will prepare you for life after graduation.\nKyungsung University is a university on the move.\nNotice\nNotice\nmore\nInterview\nNatalia Roza Krasniewska &\nAnna Izabela Krasniewska\nHospitality and Tourism Management\nWe always knew that life is about experiencing new things and following the dreams. In the time when we discovered South Korea we realized that it can be perfect place to do both. As a sisters we always enjoy doing things together. That’s why two of us study in English at the same major which is Hospitality and Tourism Management in Kyungsung University. Our plan is to open polish style café to introduce our culture to Korean people. Everyone knows that main reason for going to university is to get an academic qualification, however we also think that the social side of things and developing as a person is equally important. What we love about university life is that you are left to make your own decisions and live by yourself, especially in so unique country like South Korea. It’s great opportunity to meet people from all over the world and makes friendships that will last forever. Language create boundaries between people but during ours studies we could also learn Korean which changed the whole living abroad experience. We explored Busan city by ourselves, from trying new food to talking with native people. For now our favourite place is Gwangalli beach where take place many wonderful festivals, like Fireworks festival, which we never forget.\n이전\n재생\n정지\n다음\nKyungsung\nNEWS\nInterview\nMy thoughts about Kyungsung University\n2022-03-16\n[English Track] The reason why I am satisfied with Kyungsung : Menendez Alvares Sara\n2021-05-25\n[English Track] Reasons for choosing Kyungsung : Sahlstroem Sofia Christine\n2021-05-25\n[English Track] I am happy to realize my dream at Kyungsung University : Natalia Roza Krasniewska & Anna Izabela Krasniewska\n2021-05-21\n[English Track] Enjoy the atmosphere of Busan at Kyungsung University! : Safira Veronica Boulahrir\n2021-05-21\nVIEW MORE\nSocial Media\n경성\nSNS\n페이스북\n인스타그램\n유투브\nBrochure\nKSU Campus\nOrganization\nOverseas Branch\nOfficial\nPartner\nIndonesia\nOffice\nChina\nOffice\nKazakhstan\nOffice\nPhilippines\nOffice\nNepal\nOffice\nBangladesh\nOffice\nPakistan\nOffice\nTOP\nWelcome to Kyungsung University 서비스메뉴\n개인정보처리방침\n이용약관\n오시는길\n인명/전화번호검색\n좌측내용 더보기\n우측내용 더보기\nCampus info.\n48434\n309, Suyeong-ro, Nam-gu, Busan, Republic of Korea\nTEL :\n051-663-4114\nFAX :\n051-051-4089\nEMAIL :\n@\nCOPYRIGHT © 2023 KYUNGSUNG UNIVERSITY ALL RIGHTS RESERVED."
